Printer illustrations in this directory
=======================================

These SVG files are NOT covered by this plugin's MIT licence.

They are product illustrations belonging to Prusa Research a.s., taken from the
Prusa Connect web application at https://connect.prusa3d.com. They are included
here so the plugin can show a recognisable illustration of each printer model
alongside its status.

Prusa Research gave permission, by email on 2026-08-17, to keep them in this
repository. No conditions were attached. They remain Prusa's property and are
not relicensed: this plugin's MIT licence does not extend to them, so anyone
reusing them elsewhere should ask Prusa rather than rely on this notice.

Before that permission was sought, the question of whether a licence grant
already existed was checked rather than assumed, on 2026-08-16, and none was
found:

  * The prusa3d GitHub organisation (80 public repositories) contains no
    repository publishing these per-model illustrations. The closest candidate,
    Prusa-Link-Web (GPL-3.0, "Prusa Web interface resources"), ships only user
    interface icons — arrows, folders, fans, cameras — and no printer artwork.
    That fits: PrusaLink runs on a single printer and never needs a model
    gallery.
  * Prusa's media assets page (prusa3d.com/page/media-assets_987) offers press
    packages of photographs and logos but states no licence terms, permissions,
    or restrictions of any kind.
  * Prusa's Open Community License covers hardware CAD files, not artwork.

Deleting this directory costs nothing but the illustrations: the plugin falls
back to generic status glyphs — see stateGlyph() in PrusaWidget.qml.

Trade marks, including the Prusa name and logo, belong to Prusa Research a.s.
This plugin is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Prusa Research.

Refreshing
----------

Run tools/fetch-printer-assets to re-download them. Connect's filenames carry a
build hash that changes on every redeploy, so the script follows the app's own
chunk graph to resolve current names rather than hardcoding URLs. Files are
stored here with the hash stripped (mk4-shKwymuv.svg becomes mk4.svg).

